# ============================================================================
# Docker build context — DENY BY DEFAULT (BUD-S81 · ADR-0008)
#
# This image is PUBLISHED to a registry (GHCR, BUD-S84), so anything that reaches
# the build context can leave the machine. The repo also holds the owner's REAL
# financial history in gitignored paths (/data/ — the ledger store and multi-MB
# backup exports) and real secrets in /.env.
#
# So the posture is inverted from .gitignore: ignore EVERYTHING, then allow back
# only the files the build actually needs. A new confidential file dropped into
# the repo is therefore excluded automatically, instead of leaking until someone
# remembers to add a rule (docs/SECURITY.md §1).
# ============================================================================
*

# --- Workspace manifests + lockfile (the reproducible install) ---
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.base.json

# --- The API: source, its build script, and its manifests ---
!apps/api/package.json
!apps/api/tsconfig.json
!apps/api/src
!apps/api/scripts

# --- The web SPA: source + the Vite build inputs ---
!apps/web/package.json
!apps/web/tsconfig.json
!apps/web/vite.config.ts
!apps/web/index.html
!apps/web/src

# --- Shared domain package (bundled into the API by esbuild) ---
!packages/domain/package.json
!packages/domain/tsconfig.json
!packages/domain/src

# --- Re-exclude anything the allow-rules above would otherwise pull back in ---
# `!apps/api/src` re-includes the whole subtree, so these must be denied AFTER it.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.local
